    "Explicit immutable member bytes, a nonempty unique document selection, expected full archive hash for reads, per-document ReqIFLimits and a positive hard expansion bound; no implicit filesystem or native target."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Compare actual generated ZIP bytes with an independently built canonical container, retaining exact XML, attachment, manifest-like and unused member bytes; derive the complete external transport manifest.",
    "Resolve each original URI reference relative to its selected XML member, preserve document identity separation and require exact actual bytes without basename/case fallback or a private mandatory ZIP manifest.",
    "Reject missing/changed bindings, invalid selected XML, unsafe members and noncanonical containers before returning data; enforce existing XML safety, portable targets and the explicit expansion bound.",
    "Require the existing explicit native attachment descriptor for XHTML projection, preserve owned returned data, propagate host failures and verify the pure codec in isolated Core/PYZ distributions.",
    "Verify local/central/end header agreement and contiguous real byte extents before any member read; reject forged sizes, overlapping or omitted data, hidden original filenames and every noncanonical metadata field.",
    "Exercise actual CRC corruption, all document URI attributes and original/fallback subtrees, exact aggregate and per-XML hard bounds, interdocument passive references, owned results and real host failures."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "ReqIFZ-Exporte MÜSSEN dasselbe kanonische ZIP-Profil wie Projektbundles verwenden.",
    "scope": "14.k.W implements the pure reqifz-container-v1 codec over the shared canonical stored ZIP kernel. Explicit selected documents and real document-relative member bindings, byte-identical roundtrip and a nonrecursive external transport manifest are covered. Existing manifest-bound work archive APIs retain their behavior. This is a partial transport proof, not a complete project export/import, loss approval, full-suite or release result. 14.k.R adds the complete hostile metadata/extent, URI and per-document/aggregate-boundary matrix; invalid original ZIP path spelling is rejected before normalization. W behavior and legacy archive errors are retained."
  },
